# Keeps the build context small. Docker copies the whole context to the daemon
# BEFORE any Dockerfile runs, so without this a `docker compose build` shipped
# 2.0 GB - 1.1 G of content/, 250 M of scratch/, 154 M of output/ - none of
# which any Dockerfile reads. It was slow rather than harmful, but it is slow on
# every single build.
#
# SCOPE: this file applies to the ROOT build context only, which is hoast-player
# (docker-compose.yml `context: .`). The other services declare their own
# contexts (./services/earshot/src, ./services/rtmp-ingest, ./services/srt-gateway,
# ./telemetry) and would each need their own .dockerignore, none of which is
# currently large enough to be worth one.
#
# WHAT THE ROOT CONTEXT ACTUALLY NEEDS, so nobody has to re-derive it before
# adding a line here: services/hoast-player/* (index.html, nginx.conf,
# vod-locations.conf, 00-logformat.conf, 15-vod-enabled.sh, check/, fonts/)
# plus hoast360/dist/ and hoast360/irs/. Everything below is outside that set.

# Media. Rebuildable or released; never read at build time.
content/

# earshot's DASH working directory. Wiped on every container start anyway.
output/

# Persistent working dir: harnesses, probe captures, one-off files.
scratch/

# Only hoast360/dist and hoast360/irs are copied; the source tree and its
# dependencies are not needed, and node_modules is by far the biggest of them.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
hoast360/src/
hoast360/dependencies/

# History and tooling.
.git/
.github/
lip-sync-test/
docs/

# Local editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
